sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant H as Handler
    participant F as Stream hub
    participant S as PageReader
    participant R as Redis
    C->>H: GET ?offset=now and live=sse
    H->>H: authorize path · validate offset and cursor · choose event encoding
    H->>F: reserve existing hub, or create confirmed subscription
    F->>R: SUBSCRIBE and confirm once for a new hub
    H->>S: ReadPage(path, offset) · capture first typed page
    S->>R: EVALSHA read.lua · metadata + optional bounded range
    S-->>H: first page · type · tail · closed · incarnation
    H->>F: seed new hub identity + tail from that page
    F-->>H: ready · no duplicate initial refresh
    H-->>C: 200 · text/event-stream · no-cache · keep-alive
    loop pages to the captured tail
        H-->>C: emit the page already held · data + control · flush
        H->>S: continuation ReadPage with same snapshot · no touch
    end
    H->>F: attach at last flushed offset
    loop append wake or 1 s safety poll
        R-->>F: wake hint, or the poll timer fires
        F->>S: one shared logical ReadPage refresh
        F-->>H: shared immutable data event
        H-->>C: data then client control offset · flush
    end
    Note over H,R: first page is after registration · no Store.Get · no :prod · no attach reread
    H-->>C: control streamClosed true → close, or cycle at 60 s
